<table border="1" cellpadding="1" cellspacing="1"><tbody><tr><td><span style="white-space:nowrap;"><strong>Statement I: </strong></span></td><td>Both carbon and silicon atoms belong to group 14.&nbsp;Both CO<sub>2</sub> and SiO<sub>2</sub> are gases and linear molecules.</td></tr><tr><td><span style="white-space:nowrap;"><strong>Statement II: </strong></span></td><td>Being electron deficient due to an incomplete octet of the central atom, both&nbsp;BCl<sub>3</sub> and AlCl<sub>3</sub> behave as Lewis acids.</td></tr></tbody></table>
&nbsp;

<table border="1" cellpadding="1" cellspacing="1"><tbody><tr><td>1.</td><td><strong>Statement I</strong> is correct; <strong>Statement II</strong> is correct.</td></tr><tr><td>2.</td><td><strong>Statement I</strong> is incorrect; <strong>Statement II</strong> is incorrect.</td></tr><tr><td>3.</td><td><strong>Statement I</strong> is correct; <strong>Statement II</strong> is incorrect.</td></tr><tr><td>4.</td><td><strong>Statement I</strong> is incorrect; <strong>Statement II</strong> is correct.</td></tr></tbody></table>
